It then enters a while loop that continues as long as `perfectSquare` is less than or equal to `n`.
In each iteration of the loop, it increments `minSquares` and calculates the next perfect square using `perfectSquare = (minSquares * minSquares)`.
The function returns `minSquares` at the end of the while loop, which is the minimum number of perfect square numbers that sum up to `n`.

public static int minPerfectSquareSum(int n) {
    int count = 0;
    while (n > 0) {
        int i = 1;
        while (i * i <= n) {
            i++;
        }
        i--;
        count++;
        n -= i * i;
    }
    return count;
}

